<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jiaozhi</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Giao Chỉ</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jiaozhi was the Chinese name for the region of the Red River delta in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>. It was a commandery under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a> after 111 BCE and, much later, a province of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming Empire</a> from 1407, when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yongle-emperor">Yongle Emperor</a> annexed Đại Việt, until 1427, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-loi">Lê Lợi</a>'s uprising forced the Ming to withdraw.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jiaozhi.jpg" alt="Jiaozhi" width="320" height="406" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Albert Herrmann &amp;amp; Georg Westermann · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mainland_Southeast_Asia_in_1415.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
